	<h2 class="item-title" itemprop="name">
			<a href="/index.php?option=com_content&amp;view=article&amp;id=747:cyclone-ditwah-nbri-at-the-forefront-of-landslide-risk-management-and-recovery&amp;catid=2&amp;Itemid=101&amp;lang=en" itemprop="url">
			Cyclone Ditwah: NBRI at the Forefront of Landslide Risk Management and Recovery		</a>
		</h2>







<p><meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8" />
<title></title>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1,maximum-scale=1,user-scalable=1" /><img src="https://link.pblc.app/pub/open/6a20ff2486a5024ca9174eab/e?notrack=1&amp;sharedVia=email" width="1" height="1" alt="spacer" /></p>
<table role="presentation" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" id="templateColumns" style="text-align: left; background-color: #f9f9f9; width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr align="center" style="display: block; padding: 0; background-color: #1e3f60;">
<td align="center" style="height: auto;">
<table role="presentation" class="sFW" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="margin: 0px auto; width: 640px;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td align="center" valign="top" style="margin: 0px auto; height: auto; overflow: hidden; background-color: #1e3f60; width: 640px;" class="sFW">
<table role="presentation" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="display: block; width: 640px;" class="sFW">
<tbody>
<tr valign="top" class="sFW" style="display: block; overflow: hidden;">
<td style="width: 100%; display: block; box-sizing: border-box; overflow: hidden; padding: 10px 10px 20px 10px;">
<table role="presentation" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="display: block; width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="display: block; background-color: #fff;">
<table role="presentation" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="display: block; width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 18px 18px 18px 18px; width: 620px;" class="templateColumnContainer">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; display: table; border-collapse: separate; overflow: hidden; flex-grow: 1;" class="sFW">
<tbody>
<tr style="width: 100%;">
<td style="width: 100%;">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 0 10px 0;" valign="top" align="center">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; text-align: center; display: block; overflow: hidden;" valign="top" align="center"><img src="https://img.pblc.app/i/1168x480x9.coords.DO.0x0-100x99,86/e7897/6a20fcfb6d681ca5e8a7a5d7_Screenshot-2026-06-04-094847.png" width="584" class="sFW" style="margin: 0 auto; display: block; width: 584px; box-sizing: border-box;" alt="untitled-design-6-718887-1" /></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 21px; text-align: left; font-family: helvetica,arial,verdana,sans-serif; color: #555; padding: 5px 0 5px 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<h1 style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: bold; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 21px; text-align: left; font-family: helvetica,arial,verdana,sans-serif; color: #555; background-color: transparent;">Cyclone Ditwah: NBRI at the Forefront of Landslide Risk Management and Recovery</h1>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 0 5px 0;" valign="top" align="center">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; padding: 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<div style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; background-color: transparent;" class="elm">
<h3>Responding to an Unprecedented Disaster</h3>
<div>Cyclone Ditwah, which affected Sri Lanka in November 2025, brought exceptionally high rainfall to many landslide-prone regions of the country, exceeding historical records and triggering one of the most widespread landslide disasters in recent decades. Through satellite image analysis and field investigations, more than 1,400 landslide incidents were identified across several districts. Over 7,300 requests related to landslide incidents affecting human settlements, public infrastructure, and transportation networks were received by the National Building Research Institute (NBRI).</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>As the country's lead technical agency for landslide disaster risk management, NBRI played a critical role before, during, and after the disaster by providing scientific guidance, early warnings, emergency assessments, and technical support for recovery and reconstruction.</div>
</div>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; background-color: transparent; border-radius: 0; text-align: center; display: block; overflow: hidden;" valign="top" align="center"><img src="https://img.pblc.app/i/1168x701x9.coords.DO.0x0-100x100/7a99e/6a2100a76d681ca5e8a7c8ec_Raifall.png" width="584" class="sFW" style="margin: 0 auto; display: block; width: 584px; box-sizing: border-box; border-radius: 0;" alt="Raifall" /></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; background-color: transparent; border-radius: 0; text-align: center; display: block; overflow: hidden;" valign="top" align="center"><img src="https://img.pblc.app/i/1168x701x9.coords.DO.0x0-100x100/64bb9/6a2101826d681ca5e8a7ce9a_map.png" width="584" class="sFW" style="margin: 0 auto; display: block; width: 584px; box-sizing: border-box; border-radius: 0;" alt="map" /></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 0 5px 0;" valign="top" align="center">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; padding: 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<div style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; background-color: transparent;" class="elm">
<div>
<h3>NBRI Landslide Early Warnings</h3>
<div>The NBRI Landslide Early Warning Centre operated continuously on a 24-hour basis throughout the disaster period. Using real-time rainfall data collected through the national Automated Rain Gauge (ARG) network and established rainfall threshold criteria, landslide early warnings were issued and updated daily.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>The first Yellow Warning was issued on 17 November 2025, followed by Amber Warnings on 21 November and Red Warnings on 26 November. These warnings enabled authorities and communities in vulnerable areas to take precautionary measures, significantly contributing to the protection of lives during the event.</div>
</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
</div>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; background-color: transparent; border-radius: 0; text-align: center; display: block; overflow: hidden;" valign="top" align="center"><img src="https://img.pblc.app/i/1168x701x9.coords.DO.0x0-100x100/1ad9f/6a2100d96d681ca5e8a7cc52_EW.png" width="584" class="sFW" style="margin: 0 auto; display: block; width: 584px; box-sizing: border-box; border-radius: 0;" alt="EW" /></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 0 5px 0;" valign="top" align="center">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; padding: 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<div style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; background-color: transparent;" class="elm">
<div>
<h3>Large-Scale Emergency Response Operations</h3>
<div>Following the onset of widespread landslides, NBRI rapidly mobilized more than 50 field teams to conduct emergency investigations and risk assessments across the most severely affected districts.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>The teams carried out:</div>
<ul data-spread="false" style="margin: 0; flex-direction: column;">
<li>Landslide investigations and rapid hazard assessments</li>
<li>Safety inspections of damaged houses and settlements</li>
<li>Evaluation of high-risk slopes and unstable terrain</li>
<li>Technical assessments of roads, railways, bridges, and public infrastructure</li>
<li>Recommendations for emergency stabilization and access management</li>
</ul>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>Despite challenging weather conditions and difficult terrain, NBRI officers worked continuously to provide timely technical advice to decision-makers at national, district, and local levels.</div>
</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
</div>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; background-color: transparent; border-radius: 0; text-align: center; display: block; overflow: hidden;" valign="top" align="center"><img src="https://img.pblc.app/i/1168x701x9.coords.DO.0x0-100x100/330f5/6a21023e6d681ca5e8a7d18f_roadnrailway.png" width="584" class="sFW" style="margin: 0 auto; display: block; width: 584px; box-sizing: border-box; border-radius: 0;" alt="roadn&amp;railway" /></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 0 5px 0;" valign="top" align="center">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; padding: 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<div style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; background-color: transparent;" class="elm">
<div>
<div>
<h3>Supporting the Recovery of Critical Infrastructure</h3>
<div>One of the most significant impacts of Cyclone Ditwah was the damage caused to Sri Lanka's transportation network. Numerous roads and railway sections were affected by landslides, slope failures, rockfalls, and debris flows.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>To support restoration efforts:</div>
<ul data-spread="false" style="margin: 0; flex-direction: column;">
<li>NBRI conducted 106 road inspections and 89 railway inspections.</li>
<li>The Road Development Authority (RDA) submitted requests for 354 landslide mitigation designs.</li>
<li>Sri Lanka Railways submitted requests for 89 mitigation designs.</li>
</ul>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>NBRI has been working closely with the RDA, Sri Lanka Railways, the Sri Lanka Army, universities, and other stakeholders to develop long-term landslide mitigation solutions aimed at restoring safe transportation connectivity across affected regions.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>Recognizing the scale of the challenge, NBRI established a dedicated unit to plan and design mitigation measures for damaged road and railway sections.</div>
</div>
</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
</div>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; background-color: transparent; border-radius: 0; text-align: center; display: block; overflow: hidden;" valign="top" align="center"><img src="https://img.pblc.app/i/1168x701x9.coords.DO.0x0-100x100/991a7/6a21027b86a5024ca9176254_unit.png" width="584" class="sFW" style="margin: 0 auto; display: block; width: 584px; box-sizing: border-box; border-radius: 0;" alt="unit" /></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 0 5px 0;" valign="top" align="center">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; padding: 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<div style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; background-color: transparent;" class="elm">
<div>
<h3>Ensuring Safe Housing and Community Recovery</h3>
<div>The disaster displaced many families and damaged hundreds of houses located in landslide-prone areas. NBRI's technical teams carried out detailed investigations to determine whether affected locations could be safely reoccupied or whether relocation was necessary.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>The Institute provided:</div>
<ul data-spread="false" style="margin: 0; flex-direction: column;">
<li>Safety assessments for damaged houses</li>
<li>Identification of high-risk areas unsuitable for reoccupation</li>
<li>Technical guidance for occupation of medium- and low-risk areas</li>
<li>Recommendations for slope stabilization and risk reduction measures</li>
<li>Technical input for resettlement planning and reconstruction activities</li>
</ul>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>These assessments have been essential in supporting government agencies and communities during the recovery process while ensuring that future disaster risks are minimized.</div>
<div>
<h3>Applying Science and Technology for Disaster Management</h3>
<div>Cyclone Ditwah demonstrated the importance of science-based disaster management. Throughout the response and recovery phases, NBRI utilized a range of advanced scientific tools and technologies, including:</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<ul data-spread="false" style="margin: 0; flex-direction: column;">
<li>Rainfall threshold-based landslide early warning models</li>
<li>GIS-based hazard mapping and risk analysis</li>
<li>Geological and geotechnical investigations</li>
<li>Drone-based surveys and remote sensing technologies</li>
<li>Satellite image interpretation and damage assessment</li>
</ul>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>NBRI also initiated advanced landslide debris flow modelling using the GrFIN analytical tool to simulate potential impacts under different rainfall scenarios in highly vulnerable areas such as Kadugannawa and Aranayaka.</div>
<div>
<h3>Building Back Better for a Resilient Future</h3>
<div>While Cyclone Ditwah caused extensive damage, it also highlighted the importance of strengthening resilience against future disasters.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>NBRI is actively pursuing a "Build Back Better" approach by:</div>
<ul data-spread="false" style="margin: 0; flex-direction: column;">
<li>Identifying safe resettlement locations for affected communities</li>
<li>Supporting the rapid rehabilitation of critical infrastructure</li>
<li>Developing improved landslide mitigation designs that consider future extreme rainfall conditions</li>
<li>Expanding landslide monitoring and early warning systems</li>
<li>Updating landslide hazard zonation maps using UAV and LiDAR technologies</li>
<li>Strengthening science-based decision support systems for disaster management</li>
</ul>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>The Institute is also exploring partnerships with international organizations and research institutions to enhance technical capacity and promote innovative solutions for disaster risk reduction.</div>
<h3>Looking Ahead</h3>
<div>Cyclone Ditwah reinforced the reality that climate change is increasing the frequency and intensity of extreme rainfall events, creating new challenges for landslide risk management. The experience demonstrated the critical importance of integrating science into disaster response, recovery, and development planning.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>As Sri Lanka continues its recovery journey, NBRI remains committed to protecting lives, safeguarding infrastructure, and supporting resilient development through scientific excellence, innovation, and collaboration.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>Together, we can build a safer and more resilient future for all.</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
</div>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
