<tr>
<td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5px 5px 5px 5px; width: 640px;" class="templateColumnContainer">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; display: table; border-collapse: separate; overflow: hidden; flex-grow: 1; background-color: #fff;" class="sFW">
<tbody>
<tr style="width: 100%;">
<td style="width: 100%;">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 0 0 5px;" valign="top" align="center">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 24px; text-align: center; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #fff; padding: 5px 0 5px 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<h1 style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: bold; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 24px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #fff; background-color: transparent;"><span style="color: #122641; font-size: 23px;">Dear Esteemed Readers,</span></h1>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: helvetica,arial,verdana,sans-serif; color: #7e838b; padding: 5px 10px 5px 10px; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<div style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: helvetica,arial,verdana,sans-serif; color: #7e838b; background-color: transparent;" class="elm">
<div style="text-align: center;">
<div style="text-align: justify;">Welcome to Volume 21 of the NBRI Newsletter, the first edition published following a landmark milestone in our institutional journey. With the enactment of the National Building Research Institute Act No. 20 of 2025, the National Building Research Institute (NBRI) was officially established as the successor to the former National Building Research Organisation (NBRO). We are proud to mark this significant transformation as we recently convened the inaugural meeting of the Board of Governors, stepping confidently into a new era of institutional growth and national service.</div>
<div style="text-align: justify;">&nbsp;</div>
<div style="text-align: justify;">This edition highlights major strides in our ongoing recovery and relief efforts following Cyclone "Ditwah", including crucial design review discussions with the Honorable Deputy Minister of Transport, Highways and Urban Development to accelerate the restoration of road and railway infrastructure. It also features bilateral discussions held with the High Commission of India and the Geological Survey of India to strengthen technical cooperation and knowledge exchange.</div>
<div style="text-align: justify;">&nbsp;</div>
<div style="text-align: justify;">Furthermore, you will find details of our cutting-edge technological interventions, including a UAV-based radiometric thermal survey conducted by the GeoAI Lab to assess environmental impacts at the Karadiyana dumping site. This volume also showcases our expanding global partnerships aimed at strengthening long-term resilience, featuring strategic collaboration with the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) on community-based disaster risk management, technical sessions with the United States Geological Survey (USGS) utilizing advanced GRFIN simulation modeling, and a high-level seminar organized together with the Asian Disaster Preparedness Center (ADPC) on international best practices for post-cyclone rehabilitation.</div>
<div style="text-align: justify;">&nbsp;</div>
<div style="text-align: justify;">In addition, this edition highlights key achievements in landslide mitigation and infrastructure recovery, including the successful completion of the critical slope stabilization project along the 101.3 km – 101.6 km section of the Southern Expressway under the RLVMMP. This intervention successfully restored public safety and normal traffic flow following a major slope failure.</div>
<div style="text-align: justify;">&nbsp;</div>
<div style="text-align: justify;">We also share insights from our knowledge-sharing initiatives, including hosting postgraduate scholars from the University of Copenhagen and continuing technical dialogue with the Australian Bureau of Meteorology to further enhance rainfall forecasting capabilities for our Landslide Early Warning Systems (LEWS).</div>
<div style="text-align: justify;">&nbsp;</div>
<div style="text-align: justify;">As we embark on this new chapter, we warmly invite you to collaborate with us in research, development, and consultancy initiatives as we work together to create a safer and more resilient built environment for all.</div>
<div style="text-align: justify;">&nbsp;</div>
<div style="text-align: justify;">We sincerely hope you enjoy reading this milestone edition and welcome your valuable feedback and ideas for our future initiatives.</div>
</div>
<div style="text-align: justify;"><br />Warm regards,<br />Eng. (Dr.) Asiri Karunawardena<br />Director General</div>
</div>
</td>
</tr>
