</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 0 5px 0;" valign="top" align="center">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; padding: 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<p style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: justify; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; background-color: transparent;">The slope stabilization project at the 101.3 km – 101.6 km section of the Southern Expressway, located between the Pinnaduwa and Imaduwa interchanges, was initiated following a major slope failure that occurred in October 2023. The failure triggered a significant debris flow onto the expressway, disrupting traffic and posing a serious threat to public safety. Considering the history of repeated slope failures, the complex ground conditions, and the sensitivity of the area, this site was selected for mitigation under the Reduction of Landslide Vulnerability by Mitigation Measures Project (RLVMMP).</p>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
