<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 0 5px 0;" valign="top" align="center">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; padding: 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<p style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; background-color: transparent;">On February 19, 2026, the National Building Research Institute (NBRI) hosted ten postgraduate students from the University of Copenhagen’s Master of Disaster Management Program. Supervised by Prof. Nishara Fernando from the University of Colombo, the visit provided these international scholars with practical exposure to Sri Lanka’s Disaster Risk Reduction (DRR) strategies, bridging the gap between academic theory and field application.</p>
