<h1 style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: bold; display: block; line-height: 1; font-size: 21px; text-align: left; font-family: helvetica,arial,verdana,sans-serif; color: #555; background-color: transparent;"><span style="font-size: 24px;">NBRI–USGS Collaboration Enhances Landslide Risk Assessment through Advanced GRFIN Modelling</span></h1>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 0 5px 0;" valign="top" align="center">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; padding: 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<p style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; background-color: transparent;">A team from the United States Geological Survey (USGS) collaborated with the National Building Research Institute (NBRI) to strengthen landslide investigations through the application of the GRFIN simulation toolset. The model was applied across extensive mountainous regions to identify and map potential debris-flow pathways, followed by field verification activities in the Aranayake area of Kegalle District. In addition, hands-on capacity-building sessions were conducted at the NBRI Early Warning Centre with the active participation of several NBRI officials.</p>
</td>
</tr>
