<h1 style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: bold; display: block; line-height: 1; font-size: 21px; text-align: left; font-family: helvetica,arial,verdana,sans-serif; color: #555; background-color: transparent;"><span style="font-size: 24px;">NBRI and JICA Convene to Strengthen Collaboration on Post-Cyclone Landslide Recovery</span></h1>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 0 5px 0;" valign="top" align="center">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; padding: 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<p style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; background-color: transparent;">In a significant step toward resilient recovery from the devastating landslides triggered by Cyclone "Ditwah", the National Building Research Institute (NBRI) hosted a productive meeting with representatives from the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA). The gathering, held on January 19, 2026, included delegates from JICA headquarters, the JICA Sri Lanka office, a team of Japanese consultants, and NBRI officers. The discussions centered on advancing technical collaboration to rehabilitate affected communities and infrastructure in Sri Lanka's central highlands.</p>
</td>
