<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; padding: 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<div style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; background-color: transparent;" class="elm">
<div>The National Building Research Institute (NBRI) held a technical discussion on post-cyclone landslide recovery and rehabilitation with representatives of the U.S. Embassy in Sri Lanka and the Montana National Guard on 26 January 2026 at the NBRI premises.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>The meeting was attended by the Director General of NBRI, Eng. (Dr.) Asiri Karunawardena, along with senior NBRI officials, and representatives from the U.S. Embassy of Sri Lanka and the Montana National Guard.</div>
</div>
