</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 0 5px 0;" valign="top" align="center">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; padding: 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<div style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; background-color: transparent;" class="elm">
<div class="xdj266r x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak x1vvkbs x126k92a">
<div dir="auto">The Honorable Deputy Minister of transport, Highways and Urban Developments, Dr. Prasanna Gunasekara, visited the National Building Research Institute (NBRI) to review the progress of technical mitigation designs aimed at restoring landslide-damaged transport infrastructure across the country.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
</div>
<div class="x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a">
<div dir="auto">More than 70 professionals, including specialists from NBRI, the Road Development Authority (RDA), the Sri Lanka Railways Department (SLR), and the Sri Lanka Army are currently working at NBRI to finalize these critical designs and cost estimates.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
</div>
</div>
