<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 21px; text-align: left; font-family: helvetica,arial,verdana,sans-serif; color: #555; padding: 5px 0 5px 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<h1 style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: bold; display: block; line-height: 1; font-size: 21px; text-align: left; font-family: helvetica,arial,verdana,sans-serif; color: #555; background-color: transparent;"><span style="font-size: 24px;">NBRI and Australian Bureau of Meteorology Discuss Collaboration to Enhance Rainfall Forecasting for Landslide Early Warning</span></h1>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 0 5px 0;" valign="top" align="center">
<table role="presentation" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; padding: 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<div style="width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; font-family: lucida sans unicode,lucida grande,sans-serif; color: #5c758e; background-color: transparent;" class="elm">
<div>The National Building Research Institute (NBRI) held a strategic discussion with the Australian Bureau of Meteorology (BoM) to explore a collaborative partnership aimed at strengthening rainfall forecasting capabilities specifically for Landslide Early Warning Systems (LEWS) and disaster resilience in Sri Lanka.</div>
<div><br />The meeting was chaired by Eng. (Dr.) Asiri Karunawardena, Director General of the NBRI, and Dr. Nadeesha Dharmasiri, General Manager - National Forecast Services at the Australian Bureau of Meteorology.</div>
<div><br />Accurate quantification of rainfall is the critical parameter in issuing timely landslide warnings. The discussion centred on deploying the Australian Community Climate and Earth-System Simulator (ACCESS), a sophisticated numerical weather prediction system, tailored specifically for the Sri Lankan region.</div>
</div>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
