<tr>
<td style="display: block; background-color: #e7eaef; padding: 0 25px 0 25px;">
<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="display: block; width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr><th style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5px 5px 5px 5px; width: 590px;" class="templateColumnContainer">
<table align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; display: table; border-collapse: separate; overflow: hidden; flex-grow: 1;" class="sFW">
<tbody>
<tr style="width: 100%;">
<td style="width: 100%;">
<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="display: inline-block; width: 100%;">
<tbody style="display: block;">
<tr valign="top" class="sFW" style="display: block;">
<td style="display: block; height: 15px;">&nbsp;</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 2px; text-align: center; font-family: lato,helvetica,arial,sans-serif; color: #4f3a2e; padding: 0 0 10px 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<div style="width: 100%; font-weight: bold; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 2px; text-align: center; font-family: lato,helvetica,arial,sans-serif; color: #4f3a2e; background-color: transparent;"><span style="font-size: 22px;">Dear Esteemed Readers,</span></div>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 0 20px 0;" valign="top" align="center">
<table align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 16px; text-align: center; font-family: lato,helvetica,arial,sans-serif; color: #756a64; padding: 0 5px 0 15px; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<div style="width: 100%; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 16px; text-align: center; font-family: lato,helvetica,arial,sans-serif; color: #756a64; background-color: transparent;">Welcome to the Volume 20 of the NBRO Newsletter, a landmark edition where we proudly reflect on a period of significant institutional transformation and national achievement in building safety and resilience.</div>
<div><br />This edition presents articles on monumental milestones, beginning with the Speaker's endorsement of the certificate on the <span style="font-weight: bold;"><span style="font-weight: bold;">National Building Research Institute Act No. 20 of 2025</span></span>, which institutionalizes our critical work. Furthermore, we feature key progress in our nation-wide safety drive, including Cabinet approval for us to lead the formulation of the long-awaited <span style="font-weight: bold;">National Building Codes for Sri Lanka</span>.&nbsp;</div>
<div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>You will also find articles detailing our proactive efforts to ensure the structural stability of national assets like the historic Nine Arch Bridge, insights from successful collaborative research projects on advanced building materials, and crucial lessons learned to enhance construction safety and compliance.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>Our dedication to research and development, paired with a comprehensive range of services, continues to establish NBRO (soon to be the National Building Research Institute) as a leader in Sri Lanka's building and construction sector. From testing and consultancy to structural and project management services, our work remains at the forefront of innovation, driving sustainable development and resilience across the nation.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>We are delighted to invite you to join hands with us in research and development or through collaborative consultancy efforts as we step into this new era, working together to create a safer built environment for all. We sincerely hope you enjoy reading this milestone edition and welcome your feedback and ideas for our future initiatives.</div>
<br />Warm regards,<br />Eng. (Dr.) Asiri Karunawardena<br />Director General</div>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
