<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 0 20px 0;" valign="top" align="center">
<table align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 16px; text-align: center; font-family: lato,helvetica,arial,sans-serif; color: #756a64; padding: 0 5px 0 15px; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<div style="width: 100%; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 16px; text-align: justify; font-family: lato,helvetica,arial,sans-serif; color: #756a64; background-color: transparent;">
<div>The National Building Research Organisation (NBRO) and the National Science Foundation (NSF) have held discussion to deepen collaboration to advance nationally significant research and development.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>At a high-level meeting held on August 12, 2025 at NBRO, representatives from both organisations explored avenues to boost NBRO’s R&amp;D programme through NSF’s funding schemes, collaborative projects, and capacity-building initiatives.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>NBRO showcased its ISO-accredited laboratories, multidisciplinary expertise, and major applied research projects, including its Annual Research Symposium. NSF outlined opportunities for NBRO scientists to secure financial and technical support, encouraging greater participation in national research programmes.</div>
</div>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
