<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 2px; text-align: center; font-family: lato,helvetica,arial,sans-serif; color: #4f3a2e; padding: 0 0 10px 0; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<div style="width: 100%; font-weight: bold; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 2px; text-align: center; font-family: lato,helvetica,arial,sans-serif; color: #4f3a2e; background-color: transparent;"><span style="font-size: 22px;">Empowering the Next Generation: "The Guardians" – A Child-Centered Landslide Risk Management Program</span></div>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<table align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 0 20px 0;" valign="top" align="center">
<table align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 16px; text-align: center; font-family: lato,helvetica,arial,sans-serif; color: #756a64; padding: 0 5px 0 15px; background-color: null;" valign="top" align="center">
<div style="width: 100%; font-weight: 400; display: block; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 16px; text-align: justify; font-family: lato,helvetica,arial,sans-serif; color: #756a64; background-color: transparent;">“The Guardians” – Child-Centered Landslide Risk Management Program was organized by the National Building Research Organisation (NBRO) with the support of the Ministry of Education. The program was successfully conducted in March 2025 across several schools located in landslide-prone areas.</div>
<div style="text-align: justify;">&nbsp;</div>
<div style="text-align: justify;">The Program aim to improve the knowledge and disaster preparedness of school children through the formation of Disaster Risk Reduction (DRR)-focused Junior Scientist Clubs, strengthen school community linkages by actively engaging students in the planning and implementation of community-based awareness campaigns in partnership with local stakeholders and build the capacity of education and DRR officials and specialists in child-centered DRR and Research &amp; Development (R&amp;D) by bridging knowledge and practice gaps through specialized training and collaborative platforms.</div>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
